Z||000000||RRobinson||02-26-2001||04:05 PM||||If you are like me, you hate the "bong bong bong" Fiero buzzer. The first thing I do when I buy a Fiero is GET RID of that stupid thing. It is easy. <P>Step 1: Look under the passenger side dash<BR>Step 2: See the big blue box? Yank it out.<BR>Step 3: Place it under rear tire<BR>Step 4: Drive over it repeatedly.<BR>Step 5: Enjoy peaceful Fiero interior.<P>This may be obvious to some of you, but I'll bet there are many Fiero owners being tortured by the dreaded "bong bong bong" at this very moment.<BR> <BR>Cheers,<BR>Ryan<BR>88 GT Red<BR>87 GT Blue<BR>87 GT Black<BR>87 SE V6 Med Red <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||02-26-2001||04:53 PM||||pulled mine when i first brought it home, in '89.<P>i think batboy has it now... can't really remember.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-26-2001||07:23 PM||||That's one solution. The notes in my cave should solve whatever is actually wrong with one or allow you to disable that dumb ____ seatbelt function.<P>I don't like not having one. Too easy to leave the parking lights on. Or leave the headlights on when the doors are locked open. Others have had people leave the hand brake on, at least part way, if it's not working. (I used to wonder how you could do that.... but then I tried it with the steering wheel in diferent positions. there is at least one for every driver that will block the lights.)||||reg||1
