Z||000017||theogre||02-27-2001||08:47 PM||||I have most of the ones from writing the cave article about them. They are easy enough to fix. All the info on that is in the cave article.(There are around 9 patents on that thing.)<P>As annunciators go this is one of the more pleasant ones. (Not that you are suposed to like any of them...) If you thought ding ding ding or BZZZZZZZZ was bad you should have heard that F'ing witch voice.... The Key is in the Ignition... Ignite this you slagging little wench. By the time it repeated itself for about the fith time you wanted to crowbar the whole car.<P>It dawned on me after I wrote the article why having the dimmer all the way off kills the chime... Truck Stop parking. This way you can silence the thing when you want to or must have the parking lights on with the key off. (I do this at truck stops and gas stations at night. especially if they aren't well lit. Old habbit... Someone at GM must have the same habbit.)||||reg||1
